      "text": "Mrs. Wilson Race Play\nType: character archetype\nAffiliation: none (self-initiated)\nDescription: A suburban white woman who discovered a profound need for racialized degradation and punishment. She actively seeks out situations where she and her husband can be \"corrected\" by Black men, using provocative racist language as a deliberate trigger to incite a dominant response. This is not an act of genuine hatred for her, but a calculated performance to fulfill her and her husband's shared fantasies of submission. Her primary motivation is the intense arousal she receives from seeing her husband dominated alongside her, pushing him further into humiliation until he verbally embraces their new dynamic.\nKey Traits: Manipulative, zealous, sexually aggressive, performs a persona of piety to mask her carnal desires, strategic use of racial slurs to provoke domination.\nMethod: Initiates contact under false pretenses (e.g., \"concerned neighbor,\" reporting a crime), quickly revealing her true purpose. Willing to debase herself publicly (e.g., doorway) to heighten the intensity of the scene. Grooms her husband to participate, ensuring his humiliation is complete and a central part of her arousal.\nRelationship with Husband: Dominant within their marriage, orchestrating their shared fantasies. She derives pleasure not just from her own submission but from watching her husband be broken and forcibly put in his place.",
